## Summary

I implemented the native **SwiftUI / HIG `RedisSignalViewerPage`** at full web parity for the P4-Apple P7 admin task.

**Delivered (51/51 parity items — 6 panels, 4 states, 41 strings):**
- `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/RedisSignalViewer{Models, PageModel, PageModel.Sample, Page, Page.Controls, Page.Table, Page.Purge, RouteRegistration}.swift` (8 files, ~1,674 LOC) — adaptive macOS+iOS, `@Observable` model + KMP-ready data-source seam, no networking in the view.
- Controls panel (vehicle picker + search + category filter + auto-refresh + Refresh/Purge/Purge-All), mode/VIN/L1 diagnostic chips, 4 stat cards, sortable name/value/type/category table with masked coordinates, and the per-vehicle + cluster-wide typed-confirm purge flow with feedback banners.
- Route wiring (`.redisSignals` in `AppRoute`, `RouteRegistration`, `TeslaSyncApp`), 44 `Localizable.xcstrings` keys, `RedisSignalViewerPageModelTests.swift` (360 LOC), +2 ledger rows, and the evidence log.

